{{also|émission|Emission}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=emission}}

===Etymology===
First attested in 1607. From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|émission|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term/t|la|ēmissiō||sending forth}}, from {{term/t|la|ēmittō||send out}}, from {{term|ex||from, out of|lang=la}} + {{term/t|la|mittō||send}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪʃən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# That which is emitted or sent out.
#: {{usex|the '''emission''' was mostly blood|lang=en}}
# The act of sending or throwing out; the act of sending forth or putting into circulation; issue.
#: {{usex|the '''emission''' of light from the sun|lang=en}}
#: {{usex|the '''emission''' of heat from a fire|lang=en}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|outsending}}

